  config-6.18.57-lordos.3-rpi-2712
      The complete .config of the build, /boot/config-6.18.57-lordos.3-rpi-2712 in the image and in the
      package (SHA-256 65f4a3edf89568fa7b11c2e48ec93aae78e00672553d8230119cd6a58b198bbf).
  build-kernel.sh
      The script that configured and built it: tools/rpi/build-kernel.sh of LordOS at commit ee1f03f4
      (tags v0.8.4-beta and later; unchanged since). It starts from Raspberry Pi's bcm2712_defconfig, enables
      Landlock, Yama, the BPF LSM, BTF and sock_diag SOCK_DESTROY, and builds the Debian package with the
      kernel's own `make bindeb-pkg`. No patch is applied to the tree.

How it was built (2026-10-27, cross-compiled on Debian 13 amd64, aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc (Debian 14.2.0-19) 14.2.0):

  LORDOS_KREV=3 RPI_KERNEL_REF=234188315037848e5b07d65b85d38edc64095caa tools/rpi/build-kernel.sh <work folder> 2712

The script adds overlays/README (from the same tree) to the package, which `make dtbs_install` leaves out.
Every revision-3 build uses this commit and this script; one made with another compiler differs from this
.config only in the compiler lines (CONFIG_CC_VERSION_TEXT, CONFIG_GCC_VERSION, …). The same tree and the
script at tags v0.8.0-beta (6.18.57-1+lordos) and v0.8.1-beta to v0.8.3-beta (6.18.57-2+lordos) built the
earlier revisions; each image carries its complete .config in /boot.
